{"id":"2702f69c-e934-42ad-b4e3-a879b89502ce","kind":"note","ref":{"span":"96153cdb3ffb70b5","key":"bablr1","file":"packages/editor/workbench/pane-native.ts","baseline":{"blob":"c8160129c5ee751c2c8c8a41e1f8e9608fb20833","start":0,"end":99},"shape":{"type":"ImportDeclaration","atoms":["import","type","{","PaneAction",",","PaneCommand",",","PaneGroup",",","PaneItem","}","from","\"","@brianjenkins94/editor-api/pane","\""]},"context":{"after":"e46e22f049b9d08c"}},"payload":{"text":"The pane's native face (ARCHITECTURE.md, *Extension points* 4, natively): a pane view's content — the same data pane-views.ts draws\nbeside the code, placed the same way — drawn with VS Code's own contribution points instead, for when there's no\npane (a desktop build) or it's hidden (`editor.pane.toggleNative`): a row as an inlay hint at the end of its line\n(its label and latest value; every cell on hover), prose as a CodeLens (its first line) and a hover (all of it),\nbuttons as CodeLenses running their commands (a menu's ways in a quick pick), a one-line input as a CodeLens asking\nfor it, a card's label as a CodeLens above its first line, and a gutter mark as an overview-ruler mark (its title on\nhover). Public API only.","wrote":["Brian Jenkins"]},"author":"local","createdAt":"2026-11-22T17:54:24.729Z","updatedAt":"2026-11-22T17:54:24.729Z"}
